- Use WooCommerce hooks, actions, and filters for customizations.
- Override WooCommerce templates in a child theme, not in the plugin.
- Register custom product types, order statuses, and checkout fields using WooCommerce APIs.
- Use the WooCommerce REST API for integrations; always require authentication and permission checks.
- Add custom settings using the WooCommerce settings API.
- Test all customizations with the latest WooCommerce version.

## Examples

```php
// Add a custom product tab
add_filter( 'woocommerce_product_tabs', function( $tabs ) {
    $tabs['custom_tab'] = array(
        'title'    => __( 'Custom Tab', 'my-plugin' ),
        'priority' => 50,
        'callback' => 'my_plugin_custom_tab_content'
    );
    return $tabs;
});
function my_plugin_custom_tab_content() {
    echo '<h2>' . esc_html__( 'Custom Tab Content', 'my-plugin' ) . '</h2>';
}
```

```php
// Override WooCommerce template in child theme
// Copy woocommerce/templates/single-product/title.php to yourtheme/woocommerce/single-product/title.php and modify as needed.
```

```php
// Secure WooCommerce REST API endpoint
add_action( 'rest_api_init', function() {
    register_rest_route( 'my-plugin/v1', '/custom', array(
        'methods' => 'GET',
        'callback' => 'my_plugin_custom_endpoint',
        'permission_callback' => function() {
            return current_user_can( 'manage_woocommerce' );
        },
    ));
});
```

